cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software in your work, please cite it using the following metadata.
type: software
title: "AgentBio: an audited drug-repurposing research pipeline for rare and neglected tropical diseases"
authors:
  - family-names: Britto
    given-names: Evan
# Date-based, because this project has no release process and inventing a
# semantic version would imply one. It previously read "benchmark-freeze-v2",
# which was wrong twice over: no such tag exists in the repository (the tags
# are benchmark-cases-v1, benchmark-cases-v2 and benchmark-freeze-v1), and
# naming the software version after a benchmark freeze told the reader the
# code was unchanged since that benchmark. It was not. 117 commits have
# touched agents/, data_sources/, main_graph.py and api/ since 2026-08-09.
#
# The benchmark artifacts ARE frozen; the code is not. Those are separate
# facts and the citation now keeps them separate.
version: "2026.10.04"
date-released: 2026-10-04
repository-code: https://github.com/groundlogic-ai-source/agentbio
license: MIT
keywords:
  - drug repurposing
  - rare diseases
  - neglected tropical diseases
  - computational biology
  - validation methodology
abstract: >-
  AgentBio is a drug-repurposing research pipeline for rare diseases and WHO
  neglected tropical diseases, with an independently validated audit layer.
  Disease coverage is the Orphanet rare-disease universe plus the 20 WHO NTDs;
  both run through the same scoring and evidence engine.

  Validation results of record, frozen and separate from the evolving code:
  rediscovery benchmark v2 (6/22 in-scope, all hits top-10, frozen 2026-08-09,
  pinned by tags benchmark-cases-v2 and benchmark-freeze-v1) and audit
  claim-set v2 (defect recall 60/60, control false-flag 2/40, frozen
  2026-08-11). The code has continued to change since those freezes; the
  artifacts have not, and validation/verify_v2_provenance.py re-derives them
  from the committed files on demand.

  Full evidence trail, published failures, and rerunnable provenance
  verification: validation/validation_campaign_dossier.md and
  validation/verify_v2_provenance.py. Research prototype; not clinically
  validated.
